      "lines": [
        "Summary: "The Great Gatsby"",
        "Jay Gatsby's life is built on one dream:",
        "winning back Daisy Buchanan. Nick Carraway,",
        "the narrator, says: "He had an extraordinary",
        "gift for hope."",
        "• Setting: Long Island, 1922 – "the Jazz Age"",
        "• Themes: the American Dream, wealth vs.",
        "class, illusion/reality",
        "• Symbol: the green light → hope & the",
        "future",
        "• Key quote: "So we beat on, boats against",
        "the current, borne back ceaselessly into",
        "the past."",
        "• Don't forget: Gatsby's real name is James",
        "Gatz; it's a well-known rags-to-riches",
        "story",
        "• Tom's affair with Myrtle Wilson →",
        "conflict",
        "Grammar: Present Perfect = have/has + past",
        "participle (e.g. I've seen it).",
      ],
